00:14:20.442 --> 00:14:21.443
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:14:21.443 --> 00:14:22.862
- But does the debt matter?

00:14:23.571 --> 00:14:25.698
- Well, I mean, the
debt matters to some,

00:14:25.698 --> 00:14:29.076
to the extent that
we have a system,

00:14:29.076 --> 00:14:30.911
it is called capitalism.

00:14:30.911 --> 00:14:32.705
And in that system,

00:14:32.705 --> 00:14:35.040
laws are telling us that
debts have to be repaid.

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:37.459
(soft music)

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:43.382
How much debt do we need
to generate $1 of GDP?

00:14:43.424 --> 00:14:47.970
For the economy to create
one extra dollar of income,

00:14:49.054 --> 00:14:54.435
we need, we are relying
on $3.30 of extra debt.

00:14:55.895 --> 00:14:57.813
(soft music)

00:14:57.813 --> 00:15:00.065
An income is basically
wages plus profits.

00:15:00.065 --> 00:15:03.402
That is what GDP is, you can
also call it differently.

00:15:03.402 --> 00:15:08.407
You can say it is value added,
created by producing stuff.

00:15:08.616 --> 00:15:12.453
- And as a result of
emphasizing on the GDP,

00:15:12.453 --> 00:15:16.916
we've ended up in a situation
where the market is going on.

00:15:16.916 --> 00:15:19.627
There is some selling,
there is some buying,

00:15:19.627 --> 00:15:23.297
but we really don't know
how well people are doing.

00:15:23.297 --> 00:15:26.091
(soft music)

00:15:26.091 --> 00:15:29.345
- [Wesley Jr.] You know, when
we were kids, $1 of debt,

00:15:29.345 --> 00:15:32.139
pretty much created $1 of GDP.

00:15:32.139 --> 00:15:33.599
- Oh wow.

00:15:33.599 --> 00:15:34.934
- So, you know, it's
like Keynesian economics,

00:15:34.934 --> 00:15:36.936
you put the money
into social projects

00:15:36.936 --> 00:15:39.146
and it recycles back
into the economy.

00:15:40.147 --> 00:15:43.776
But today it takes
more than $3 of debt

00:15:43.776 --> 00:15:45.486
